# SAEA-E21-OBS-E1-SPEAKER-TURN-UNITS-V1 - the Earnings-21 OBS cell of the
# 2026-09-05 three-dimension program
# (docs/readiness/2026-09-07-e21-obs-speaker-turn-units-v1-preregistration.md).
#
# NOT AUTHORIZED AND NOT COMPOSABLE. This file is a launch record, not a
# permission, and it cannot be launched today even with one: the baseline
# fragment carries obs_unit_plan, obs_unit_plan_sha256 and
# obs_slice_tail_silence_seconds, and ObsLoopConfig.from_values rejects every
# unknown obs_ key fail-closed. The seam is specified in section 8 of the
# preregistration and is implemented AFTER wt/ts2y's tail knob merges, because
# the cutter calls reproduction.obs_audio.encode_slice. The cell then needs a
# passing seam falsifier, a 4-row dry run, its own exposure row and the owner's
# GO.
#
# Same population, same split identity, same D1 identity, same model fragment,
# same serving geometry (-c 36864 -np 6, GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_GRAPHS=1), same
# greedy decoding, same build, same audio path and the same instruction byte for
# byte as the sealed comparator SAEA-E21-FULL44-DIRECT-BASELINE-V2. ONE factor
# moves: the TRANSPORT UNIT. Instead of ceil(D/90) fixed windows off the clock,
# the OBS loop cuts each call into the hash-pinned v2 plan's speaker-turn
# units (schema saea-e21-speaker-turn-units-v2, re-pinned 2026-09-08 under
# the coordinator's minimum-duration merge rule) -- 5,122 over the 44 calls
# against 1,593 windows, 11.0 % of them ending on an active frame against
# 65.5 %, 76.1 % of them carrying exactly one speaker against 40.5 %, and
# ZERO left under the 1.0 s minimum (v1's own 5,288-unit plan carried 166).
#
# The units and the windows do NOT align one to one, so the cell pairs at the
# CALL (44 clusters, seed 20260903, CI90) and makes no paper-facing
# effectiveness claim; and a contact-matched control is impossible by
# construction. Both facts are stated in the preregistration before any number
# is read.
